## Inherited listener trait crosswalk

- Compared the public Rust trait inventory with compatibility matrices. The
  concurrent and orderly listener traits were the only public Rust traits
  without their exact Java interface method recorded in those matrices.
- Read the pinned Java `MessageListenerConcurrently` and `MessageListenerOrderly`
  declarations and `ConsumeRequest.run` call sites. Both inherit only the
  methodless `MessageListener` marker and declare one callback. Existing Rust
  flows preserve the queue/context ownership; concurrent absent-status or
  panic maps to retry, and orderly absent-status or panic maps to suspension.
- Added method-level Java-to-Rust rows to Phase 10 and Phase 12, with links to
  the existing context/status and callback tests. No missing capability was
  confirmed in this trait slice; broad P18-V01 remains open.
- After the selector implementation commits, PASS:
